1
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:37,360
Excuse me. My name is Richard Stewart.

2
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:38,790
I'm a photographer.

3
00:00:38,790 --> 00:00:40,480
May I take a picture of you and your little boy?

4
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:41,340
What's it for?

5
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:41,870
It's for a book.

6
00:00:41,870 --> 00:00:42,410
Richard Stewart, 46 Linden Street,

7
00:00:42,410 --> 00:00:44,110
You're writing a book?

8
00:00:44,110 --> 00:00:45,470
It's a book of pictures.

9
00:00:45,470 --> 00:00:47,160
I call it Family Album, U.S.A.

10
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:49,230
Oh, that's a nice idea.

11
00:00:49,230 --> 00:00:51,160
Well, it's fine if you take our picture.

12
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:52,740
I'm Martha Vann.

13
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:55,820
Thank you. I appreciate your help.

14
00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:57,740
I'm Richard. What's your name?

15
00:00:57,740 --> 00:00:58,920
Gerald.

16
00:00:58,920 --> 00:00:59,850
How old are you, Gerald?

17
00:00:59,850 --> 00:01:00,990
Five.

18
00:01:00,990 --> 00:01:01,980
And where do you live?

19
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:03,510
We live in California.

20
00:01:03,510 --> 00:01:07,220
Well, welcome to New York.

21
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:10,700
OK, just a second.

22
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:12,370
I'm almost ready here.

23
00:01:12,370 --> 00:01:13,730
Can I help you?

24
00:01:13,730 --> 00:01:21,690
Oh, please.

25
00:01:21,690 --> 00:01:28,460
Hold Gerald's hand, please. Great!

26
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:32,770
Now point to the buildings.

27
00:01:32,770 --> 00:01:36,390
Terrific!

28
00:01:36,390 --> 00:01:43,640
Give Mommy a kiss, Gerald. Nice!

29
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:45,900
Thank you, Gerald.

30
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:47,570
And thank you, Mrs. Vann.

31
00:01:47,570 --> 00:01:48,380
Oh, my pleasure.

32
00:01:48,380 --> 00:01:50,160
We'll be looking for your book.

33
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:56,230
Thank you. Good-bye. Bye, Gerald.

34
00:01:56,230 --> 00:01:58,260
Thanks again.

35
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:00,030
Oh, you're welcome.

36
00:02:00,030 --> 00:02:01,880
Hey, let me take your picture!

37
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:10,100
Wonderful. Please.

38
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:11,430
Are you from New York?

39
00:02:11,430 --> 00:02:13,150
No, I'm from Greece.

40
00:02:13,150 --> 00:02:15,780
I'm an exchange student.

41
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:17,260
When did you come here?

42
00:02:17,260 --> 00:02:18,900
Three months ago.

43
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:20,710
Your English is very good.

44
00:02:20,710 --> 00:02:22,250
Thanks.

45
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:28,710
I studied English in school.

46
00:02:28,710 --> 00:02:30,010
Would you like some coffee?

47
00:02:30,010 --> 00:02:32,160
No, thank you.

48
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:34,150
Tell me about your book.

49
00:02:34,150 --> 00:02:36,190
Oh, it's not finished yet,

50
00:02:36,190 --> 00:02:37,750
but I have some of the pictures.

51
00:02:37,750 --> 00:02:38,780
Would you like to see them?

52
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:40,700
Yes. I'd like that.

53
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:48,070
Here they are. Family Album, U.S.A.

54
00:02:48,070 --> 00:02:50,210
It's an album of pictures of the United States:

55
00:02:50,210 --> 00:02:53,460
the cities, the special places, and the people.

56
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:56,310
And these are pictures of people working:

57
00:02:56,310 --> 00:03:06,540
steelworkers, bankers, police, street vendors,

58
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:11,030
ambulance drivers, doctors....

59
00:03:11,030 --> 00:03:16,320
Oh, this is my father. He's a doctor.

60
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:17,810
This is my mother.

61
00:03:17,810 --> 00:03:18,580
What's her name?

62
00:03:18,580 --> 00:03:21,830
Ellen.

63
00:03:21,830 --> 00:03:23,280
My younger brother, Robbie.

64
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:25,580
He goes to high school.

65
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:27,400
This is my sister Susan.

66
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:31,060
She works for a toy company.

67
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:35,190
Here's my grandfather. He lives in Florida.

68
00:03:35,190 --> 00:03:37,240
And this is my wife Marilyn.

69
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:38,630
Oh, she's very pretty.

70
00:03:38,630 --> 00:03:42,350
Thanks. And what about your family?

71
00:03:42,350 --> 00:03:44,850
They are in Thessaloniki.

72
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:47,370
That's a large city in northern Greece.

73
00:03:47,370 --> 00:03:50,270
But now I'm living in the Bronx.

74
00:03:50,270 --> 00:03:51,960
With a Greek-American family?

75
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:57,910
No. Hispanic.

76
00:03:57,910 --> 00:04:01,740
Oh no! It's five thirty.

77
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:02,770
Will you excuse me?

78
00:04:02,770 --> 00:04:05,110
I have to meet my wife.

79
00:04:05,110 --> 00:04:06,390
It was nice meeting you.

80
00:04:06,390 --> 00:04:08,190
It was a pleasure meeting you, too.

81
00:04:08,190 --> 00:04:09,670
Thanks for your help.

82
00:04:09,670 --> 00:04:12,390
And good luck! I've got to go.

83
00:04:12,390 --> 00:04:13,960
By the way, I'm Richard.

84
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:14,710
What's your name?

85
00:04:14,710 --> 00:04:16,220
Alexandra.

86
00:04:16,220 --> 00:04:17,100
Bye-bye, Alexandra. Thanks.

87
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:20,100
Bye-bye. Richard! Richard! You left your bag!
